# NEOCOM Git conventions

Primary owner: `/neocom-git`. Detail skill: `/neocom-git-workflow`. Git slash commands: `/git:commit <project>` commits pending work on the current branch; `/git:pr` commits and prepares pull requests for one project, or for every active repository when no project is given.

## Commits

```text
<type>(<scope>): <short summary>

<optional body — why>

<optional footer>
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `style`, `perf`, `revert`  
Scopes (examples): `front`, `meta`, `back`, `openspec`, `root`, `infra`, `login`, `init`

- Imperative mood; body explains **why**
- HEREDOC for `git commit -m`; no secrets
- Commit only when asked, when `/git:commit` or `/git:pr` is invoked, or when `/neocom-git` is invoked to commit
- No amend unless user rules allow; no force push to main/master; never update git config

## PRs

- `gh pr create` with **Summary** + **Test plan**
- Push `-u` when needed
- A pull request into `develop` uses a Conventional Commit title or the branch purpose
- A pull request from `develop` into `main` is titled `Release-` plus GitVersion `MajorMinorPatch` (`Release-0.1.0`). Calculate it with `gitversion /nocache /showvariable MajorMinorPatch` on a temporary `main` checkout after merging `develop`. Do not push that merge
- **Mandatory before any pull request:** sync the package version. For **`neocom-front`**, run `npm run version:sync` from GitVersion `MajorMinorPatch` (updates `package.json`, both `appVersion` fields, `index.html` loading text, Cypress version expectation, and `.app-banner.txt`), commit those files if they changed, then open the PR. For **`neocom-back`**, run `npm run version:sync` (GitVersion) and commit when `package.json` version changes. For **`neocom-domain`**, run `npm run version:sync` to pull the latest **npm** published version into `package.json` (npm-led; do not use GitVersion for this library). Do not open a PR with a stale version.
- Name the repository and any OpenSpec changes
- Do not update a submodule pointer. `neocom` is deprecated

## Releases

- Branches: `feat/…` (or `feature/…` when user-mandated), `fix/…`, `release/x.y.z`; tags: `vX.Y.Z`
- **`neocom-meta`:** default `feature/agents` (general agents/docs/OpenSpec behaviour). `feature/cicd` only for CI/CD ecosystem work; when commanded, rebase onto latest `feature/agents` or `develop`. See `.cursor/templates/branch-names.md`
- On a new **`neocom-front`** `feature/…` branch, run `npm run version:sync` early; it is also mandatory again before the pull request
- Checklist: version synced, tests green, OpenSpec status noted, release stays in the owning repository
- Align with L2 `INFRA-036`…`INFRA-039`; do not invent undeclared deploy targets
